### Fix imago/jupyter display against current imago PNG API

jupyter/jupyter.lisp still calls the long-gone IMAGO-PNGIO package
(old write-png-to-stream interface).  Current imago (src/file-png.lisp,
src/package.lisp:74) exports WRITE-PNG-TO-STREAM in the IMAGO package
(zpng backend, same (image stream) lambda list).  Port the display
method to it so show-image emits a real encoded PNG — no alias or shim
introduced; binary images still funnel through grayscale conversion.

--- a/jupyter/jupyter.lisp
+++ b/jupyter/jupyter.lisp
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@
 (defmethod show-image ((image image))
   (png
    (usb8-array-to-base64-string
     (flexi-streams:with-output-to-sequence (stream)
-      (imago-pngio:write-png-to-stream image stream)))))
+      (imago:write-png-to-stream image stream)))))
 
 (defmethod show-image ((image binary-image))
   (show-image (convert-to-grayscale image)))
